# Paths owned by the factory (dsf-base plus the workflow layer of this dsf-* repo).
#
#   dsf-base  ->  dsf-<workflow>  ->  application
#
# An application repo uses this file to tell factory changes from application
# changes. `scripts/dsf/dsf-sync.sh contribute` sends commits that touch only these
# paths back to the dsf-* repo the application was cloned from.
# Everything not matched here belongs to the application and never leaves it.
#
# Pattern rules: see base.paths.

.dsf/
!.dsf/settings/app.json
!.dsf/modes.app.json
.dsf.layer
.claude/
!.claude/settings.local.json
!.claude/skills/app-
!.claude/agents/app-
!.claude/commands/app-
=.claude/settings.json
.specify/
=.specify/memory/constitution.md
scripts/dsf/
config/dsf/
docs/dsf/
docs/workflow/
.github/workflows/dsf-
CLAUDE.md
Makefile
Makefile.workflow
cloneForApplication.sh
base.paths
dsf.paths
=README.md
=.gitignore
=LICENSE
